      "field_name": "other_symptoms_established",
      "value": "ophthalmoplegia; tetraparesis; hyperreflexia; babinski; clonus; urinary retention; central hypoventilation; neuropathic pain; allodynia",
      "quote": "There was a complex ophthalmoplegia, tetraparesis, hyper-reflexia with extensor plantars, clonus at the ankles and knees, and urinary retention requiring catheterization. She developed nocturnal apneic episodes due to central hypoventilation and extensor spasms of the lower limbs. Simultaneously, she developed worsening severe neuropathic pain that was constant and described as \"electric shocks\" throughout both lower limbs and abdomen. Marked mechanical allodynia was noted, with light touch described as \"excruciating\" and \"like electric barbed wire.\"",
      "confidence": "high"
